    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Description\n\nHello,\n\nnvim version 0.12.3, nvim-lspconfig commit bfcc0171 (19th june).\n\nCurrently the recognized filetypes for clangd LSP are defined as (see `clangd.lua`):\n\n    filetypes = { 'c', 'cpp', 'objc', 'objcpp', 'cuda' },\n\nAs a result, C files that are detected as `c.doxygen` type will not have the LSP attached.\n\nThe simple fix is to update the config for clangd in `~/.vim/init.lua`, like\n\n    vim.lsp.config('clangd', {\n      filetypes = { 'c', 'c.doxygen', 'cpp', 'objc', 'objcpp', 'cuda' },\n    })\n \nIdeally this configuration should be done in `clangd.lua` so that all users have it by default.",
    "closed_at": "2026-06-25T17:57:51Z",
